-- title:
--   Finitely many vectors span V modulo its unipotent coinvariants
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a nonzero prime ideal of the ring of integers of $\mathbb{Q}$, write $F$ for the $p$-adic completion of $\mathbb{Q}$, and let $V$ be a $\mathbb{C}$-submodule of the space of all functions $\mathrm{GL}_2(F) \to \mathbb{C}$. Assume: (i) $V$ is stable under right translation, i.e. for $W \in V$ and $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(F)$ the function $g \mapsto W(gh)$ lies in $V$; (ii) each $W \in V$ is smooth, in the sense that there is an open subgroup $U \le \mathrm{GL}_2(F)$ with $W(gk) = W(g)$ for all $k \in U$ and all $g$; (iii) $V$ is admissible, in the sense that for every open subgroup $U$ there is a finite set $B$ of functions $\mathrm{GL}_2(F) \to \mathbb{C}$ such that every $W \in V$ satisfying $W(gk) = W(g)$ for all $k \in U$, $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(F)$ lies in the $\mathbb{C}$-span of $B$ (the members of $B$ are not required to lie in $V$); (iv) $V$ is irreducible, in the sense that for every nonzero $W_0 \in V$ each $W \in V$ lies in the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the right translates $g \mapsto W_0(gh)$, $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(F)$. The conclusion is that there is a finite set $S$ of functions with $S \subseteq V$ such that every $W \in V$ admits coefficients $c$, a complex-valued function on the space of all functions $\mathrm{GL}_2(F)\to\mathbb{C}$, for which $W - \sum_{s \in S} c(s)\, s$ lies in the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the set of functions $g \mapsto W'(g\, n(t)) - W'(g)$ with $W' \in V$ and $t \in F$, where $n(t)$ denotes the upper triangular unipotent matrix $\begin{pmatrix} 1 & t \\ 0 & 1\end{pmatrix}$ viewed in $\mathrm{GL}_2(F)$.
--
--   This is the finiteness statement for the unipotent coinvariants (Jacquet module) $V/V(N)$ of an irreducible admissible smooth space of functions on $\mathrm{GL}_2(F)$ under right translation, formulated as: finitely many elements of $V$ span $V$ modulo the subspace generated by the differences $R(n(t))W' - W'$. It is used in the analysis of Whittaker models for the local components at $p$, being cited by [`AutomorphicForm.WhittakerModel.apply_mul_apply_eq_apply_mul_apply_of_forall_diagOne_eq_smul_of_transcendental`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.WhittakerModel.apply_mul_apply_eq_apply_mul_apply_of_forall_diagOne_eq_smul_of_transcendental).
